# There is no single .env for this repo. Configuration lives in three places:
#
# 1. backend/ (Cloudflare Worker)
#    - Plain settings: backend/wrangler.toml ([env.production.vars])
#    - Secrets: npx wrangler secret put NAME --env production
#      Required: JWT_SECRET
#      Optional until the feature is used: RESEND_API_KEY (email),
#        STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (payments),
#        SOCIAL_TOKEN_KEY + META_APP_SECRET (Facebook/Instagram),
#        VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY + VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY (web push: npm run push:keys:prod),
#        YT_CLIENT_ID + YT_CLIENT_SECRET (YouTube), PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN (merch)
#    - Local development: backend/.dev.vars (git-ignored), same names.
#
# 2. mobile/ (the app): copy mobile/.env.example to mobile/.env.
#    Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* values go into the app, so never put secrets there.
#
# 3. web-app/ (the website): NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE at build time (defaults to
#    the live API); BACKEND_API_BASE in web-app/wrangler.jsonc.
#
# See START_HERE.md for what each one does.
